message: "If you use this software, please cite the repository."
title: "Environment Snapshots in Mårran: Taming Mutation under Non-Strict Evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Liddell"
    given-names: "Alice Eve"
    alias: "Fancryer"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1304-0984"
    affiliation: "University of Electronic Science and Technology of China"
version: 0.2.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: https://github.com/Fancryer/Marran
abstract: >-
  Mårran is an experimental statically typed programming language exploring the
  interaction between non-strict evaluation, controlled mutation and algebraic
  effects. A binding qualifier imm evaluates a delayed computation in a snapshot
  of the environment, in which data is copied and reachable code is frozen so
  that it neither creates nor observes mutable state. This artifact contains the
  implementation, the type-and-effect inference engine, the interpreter, the
  test suite and the Criterion benchmark harness.
keywords:
  - programming languages
  - non-strict evaluation
  - mutable state
  - effect systems
  - snapshots
